# Lexa fixes on top of main 911377d (merge with git merge-file)

Files are full versions based on 911377d. In the repo root run:

    for f in $(cat FILES.txt); do
      git show 911377d:$f > /tmp/base
      git merge-file $f /tmp/base lexa-fix/$f
    done
    npx tsc --noEmit

What changed
- social-client.ts: errText() (English network errors such as "Failed to fetch" are never shown), error state in useTCourses and usePublicLibrary, formal error texts.
- PublicLibraryView: a failed load shows an error with a retry button, not "no courses in this category"; the add/remove button updates right away after removing (stale "in library"); guests see the right state; button text «افزودن به کتابخانهٔ من / در کتابخانهٔ من»; formal, plain wording.
- OrgView + orgs.ts: the directory, the centre content tab, members and "my invitations" show an error with retry instead of a false empty state ("no centre yet", "no teacher yet"); members failure no longer hides the manager tabs; "اولین باشید!" removed; remaining informal texts made formal.
- FeedBell: loading and error states, «مدرسان».
- handlers.ts: «در پاسخ به …» survives a reload (replyToUsername in getPost); centre logo upload only for an active owner/manager or admin; formal upload errors.
- PostView: formal texts.

Still for Z (files I could not rebuild byte-exact)
- DashboardView: feed block uses useSocial().error (error + retry instead of "nothing published"); drop «تا تازه‌هایش این‌جا بدرخشد».
- StudioView: courses tab uses useTCourses().loading/error (spinner/retry instead of "no courses yet").
- TeachersView: disable the follow button while its request runs (double-tap flips the state).
- CourseView: the signed-in add-to-library POST must check res.ok and show the error.
- studio-widgets ThumbnailPicker: reject /api/ paths and drop the "/api/cover/…" placeholder.
